{
  "version": 1,
  "source": "DIDSA-CAD client/lib/sketch/label_drag_resolver.dart (distance, line distance, radius, two-line angle) and client/lib/sketch/dimension_types.dart (the part D types), as the flat app's label drag and click-to-drop use them. Contract: DIDSA-VR docs/dimension-constraint-parity-plan.md section 3.2. Checked by client/test/sketch_label_placement_cases_test.dart.",
  "units": "Sketch units (millimetres on the wire); angles in degrees; points as [x, y] in the sketch plane.",
  "tolerance": 1e-09,
  "notes": [
    "placement is what PUT .../constraints/{id}/label saves (only the fields the kind uses); null means the pointer gives no placement and the label stays where it was.",
    "label_center is where that placement lays out the label's centre. It equals the pointer except where a kind says otherwise (arc_length near the centre, rounding)."
  ],
  "kinds": {
    "distance_linear": "A distance between Points A and B (a line's length, an aligned point pair, a centre distance). offset: how far the dimension line sits from A-B along its left-hand normal (A-B turned 90 degrees counter-clockwise); along: the label's distance from the dimension line's midpoint towards B. Label centre = mid(A,B) + n*offset + t*along.",
    "distance_horizontal": "offset: the dimension line's y past max(A.y, B.y); along: the label's x from the points' mid x (positive right). Label centre = (mid.x + along, max(A.y,B.y) + offset).",
    "distance_vertical": "offset: the dimension line's x past max(A.x, B.x); along: the label's y from the points' mid y (positive up). Label centre = (max(A.x,B.x) + offset, mid.y + along).",
    "point_line_distance": "distance_linear from the Point (A) to its foot on the line's infinite extension (B).",
    "ellipse_axis": "A full ellipse's radius or diameter along an axis: distance_linear from the opposite tip (A) to the tip the dimension names (B). An elliptical arc has no opposite tip: its axes use radius (centre, axis tip).",
    "line_distance": "Two parallel lines. With u = line 1's unit direction, n = the unit normal from line 1 towards line 2, midA = line 1's midpoint, midB = its foot on line 2: offset = (P - midA).u; along = (P - mid(midA,midB)).n. Label centre = mid(midA,midB) + u*offset + n*along.",
    "radius": "Circle or arc (rim = the circle's radius Point, an arc's start). angle: the leader's direction in degrees counter-clockwise from the rim Point's direction, in (-180, 180]; leg: the label's distance beyond the circle (negative inside). Label centre = centre + (r + leg) at (rim angle + angle).",
    "diameter": "Same fields and rule as radius.",
    "angle": "Two lines (AngleConstraint). The vertex is where the lines' extensions meet; each outward ray points from it towards its line's midpoint. quadrant bit 0 flips ray 1, bit 1 flips ray 2; no quadrant: ray 2 flips when the outward angle is nearer 180 - value_degrees than value_degrees. radius: the arc's radius (the pointer's distance from the vertex); along: the label's distance ALONG THE ARC from the arc's middle, positive towards ray 2. No placement (null) when the pointer is behind the vertex (its direction has a dot product <= 0 with the arc's middle) or on it.",
    "arc_length": "leg: how far outside the arc the dimension arc runs (negative inside); angle: the label's place along it, degrees counter-clockwise from the arc's middle, in (-180, 180]. The dimension arc's radius is max(r + leg, 0.1 r), so a pointer within a tenth of the radius of the centre puts the label on that smallest arc, not at the pointer.",
    "horizontal_angle": "quadrant bit 0: the angle is drawn at the line's end (else its start); bit 1: the horizontal ray is -x (else +x). Ray 1 runs along the line from that vertex, ray 2 is the horizontal. radius: the pointer's distance from the vertex; angle: degrees counter-clockwise from the middle of the arc that runs the short way from ray 1 to ray 2, in (-180, 180].",
    "point_angle": "Three Points, the vertex first. quadrant bit 0 flips ray 1 (vertex to point 1), bit 1 ray 2 (vertex to point 2). radius and angle as horizontal_angle.",
    "point_circle_distance": "distance_linear between the Point (A) and the circle's point on the line through the Point and the centre (B): the nearer one for side min, the farther one for max.",
    "circle_distance": "distance_linear between each circle's point on the centre line (A on circle 1, B on circle 2): facing each other for side min (the gap), facing away for max.",
    "line_circle_distance": "distance_linear from the centre's foot on the line (A) to the circle's point square to the line (B): towards the line for side min (tangent side), away from it for max (far side)."
  },
